<p class="eyebrow">FOR WOMEN WHO’VE HAD A HARD FEW YEARS</p>
<h1 style="font-family:'Source Serif 4',Georgia,serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(30px,7.2vw,42px);line-height:1.12;color:#1F2419">7 Signs Your Body Stopped Clearing Things Out <span class="hl">After a Hard Few Years</span></h1>
<p class="t" style="font-size:20px">You eat clean, keep moving, try everything, and still wake up puffy. If the last few years asked a lot of you (a divorce, a betrayal, caring for everyone but yourself), your body may still be carrying it. Count how many of these sound like you.</p>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#5E6656">By the Resilia editorial team · Updated November 2026 · 3 min read</p>
<img src="{{ 't06b-hero.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="A woman looking at her puffy face in the bathroom mirror in the morning" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;object-fit:cover;border-radius:14px">
<section class="sec" style="border-top:0;padding-top:0">
<div class="sign"><div class="num">1</div><div><h3>Puffy face first thing in the morning</h3><p>Overnight your body clears what the day left behind. When that slows, you wake up puffy.</p></div></div>
<div class="sign"><div class="num">2</div><div><h3>Your jawline isn&#x27;t where it used to be</h3><p>The face is often where a slow clean-up shows first.</p></div></div>
<div class="sign"><div class="num">3</div><div><h3>Your belly feels hard and swollen by afternoon</h3><p>What isn&#x27;t moved along tends to settle around the middle.</p></div></div>
<div class="sign"><div class="num">4</div><div><h3>You&#x27;re done for the day by 6pm</h3><p>Feeling heavy all day is exhausting in itself.</p></div></div>
<div class="sign"><div class="num">5</div><div><h3>What used to work doesn&#x27;t move anything</h3><p>You can&#x27;t diet away what&#x27;s just sitting there.</p></div></div>
<div class="sign"><div class="num">6</div><div><h3>You wake at 3am and can&#x27;t switch off</h3><p>Your body does much of its clearing during deep sleep, and stress cuts it short.</p></div></div>
<div class="sign"><div class="num">7</div><div><h3>There&#x27;s a dress you&#x27;ve stopped trying on</h3><p>It&#x27;s not discipline you&#x27;re missing.</p></div></div>
<div class="box" style="text-align:center"><p style="font-size:19px;font-weight:800">3 or more?</p><p class="t" style="font-size:17px">You’re not imagining it, and you’re not failing. Here’s what’s likely going on.</p></div>
</section>
<section class="sec"><h2 class="h2">Your body has a clean-up system almost nobody talks about.</h2>
<img src="https://resilia.shop/cdn/shop/files/hf_20260803_191106_e4857c9a-536a-44b7-a4f9-d39a8ad4175a.png?v=1785785207&width=700" alt="Illustration of the lymphatic system" style="width:60%;margin:0 auto;aspect-ratio:3/4;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;background:#F7F9F4">
<p class="t">Your lymphatic system works alongside your bloodstream to move excess fluid, help clear waste and carry dietary fats from your gut.</p>
<p class="t">It has no pump of its own. It moves with your muscles, your breathing and your sleep.</p>
<p class="t">Long days, short nights, sitting and stress slow it down, and often it starts with a gut that&#x27;s out of balance. What should move along sits in the face, belly and ankles.</p>
<p style="font-size:12px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#3F5A1E;margin-top:4px">THE LOOP · EACH STEP FEEDS THE NEXT</p>
<div class="loop"><div>Stress and short nights pile up</div><div>Gut balance slips</div><div>Digestion slows, meals feel heavier</div><div>Bloat and fluid build</div><div>You feel puffy, heavy and tired</div><div>You move less and sleep worse</div></div>
</section>
<section class="sec"><h2 class="h2">Break the loop at the source.</h2><p class="t">Eating less, cutting wine, fat burners, probiotics: each one misses the start of the loop. The gut, its balance and the inflammation come first.</p>
<p style="font-size:12px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#3F5A1E">TWO OILS. TWO JOBS. ONE SOFTGEL ROUTINE.</p>
